(a) A graduate applies for a job in two firms X and Y the probability of him being selected in firm X is 0.7 and being rejected at Y is 0.5. The probability of at least one of his applications being rejected is 0.6. Determine the probability that he will be selected by one of the firms. **(5 Marks)**

(b) X and Y are two events such that $P(X/Y) = 0.4$, $P(Y) = 0.25$ and $P(X) = 0.2$
Find:

(i) $P(Y/X)$ **(3 Marks)**
(i) $P(X \cap Y)$ **(3 Marks)**
(ii) $P(X \cup Y)$ **(3 Marks)**

(c) A fruit seller found out that out of 100 apples in a box, 10 were bad and could not be sold. Three fruits are drawn at random by a customer, one at a time, replacing the previous one each time. Find the probability that at least one of the apples is bad. **(6 Marks)**

